1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,540
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:21,900
It's been many years since the last time I set foot on this ground.

3
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:30,280
Oh, great lord, please, grant the people comfortable lives and dignified deaths.

4
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:58,900
Thank you.

5
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:28,880
Let's go.

6
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:58,880
Let's go.

7
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:28,880
Let's go.

8
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:30,660
About the Demon Sword.

9
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:37,560
He surrendered to us after the battle under the school, so we've taken him into custody.

10
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,540
But I think you should be the one to decide how he's dealt with now that we have him.

11
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:44,100
Yes, I should.

12
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,140
Is there something bothering you, sir?

13
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:49,600
Yes.

14
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,940
There's something strange about the Demon Sword.

15
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,180
What do you mean by strange?

16
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:59,640
The Demon Sword has devoured a great number of human souls, right?

17
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:03,440
So we'd expect him to be well on his way to becoming a key ship.

18
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:08,300
But nothing could be further from the truth.

19
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,680
What do you mean?

20
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:17,420
I don't know how it's even possible, but I guess you could say it seems like something has had a sort of purifying effect on him recently.

21
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:20,500
What do you think about it, Sid?

22
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,500
I don't have the slightest idea.

23
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:27,220
But I do think we need to hold the Demon Sword accountable for all the horrible things he's done.

24
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:32,400
I realize he's a child and he was led by a witch, but we can't ignore his actions.

25
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:38,280
I think the same severe punishment that we always use for cases like this should apply here as well.

26
00:03:38,740 --> 00:03:39,700
Don't you agree?

27
00:03:46,420 --> 00:03:47,200
Don't know.

28
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:49,080
So I think I'm going to put it off.

29
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,900
The Death Scythes convene.

30
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,760
Stop Dad's staff reassignment?

31
00:03:57,220 --> 00:04:00,780
Hey, what are you doing?

32
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,300
Just come on.

33
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:03,620
I'm not coming anywhere.

34
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:07,360
Lord Death specifically told us to stay put until our injuries are all healed.

35
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:08,380
Seriously.

36
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:11,580
If you stay put any longer than you already have.

37
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:15,460
Look, you'll start sprouting mushrooms and that's not cool.

38
00:04:15,460 --> 00:04:16,360
I will not!

39
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:17,600
Oh, come on.

40
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,600
You know you want to.

41
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,020
What are you planning, soul?

42
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,140
Just a little change of pace.

43
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:23,240
Huh?

44
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:24,540
Yo!

45
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:32,240
On to the next issue.

46
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:38,060
Including Spirit, what's our head count looking like so far for the gathering of the eight Death Scythes?

47
00:04:38,460 --> 00:04:41,420
Well, it appears that Justin has now arrived.

48
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:45,320
Counting Spirit and the other two that got in earlier, we have a total of four.

49
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:47,940
Okay, we've got half of them at least.

50
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,280
What are the other four up to?

51
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:54,620
It looks like the ones in charge of Europe and West Asia are too busy with work and can't make it here right now.

52
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:55,900
That's no good.

53
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:58,620
What about the one we've got stationed down in South America?

54
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:02,100
It's kind of hard to tell with all the growling and barking.

55
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,380
And Africa?

56
00:05:03,380 --> 00:05:05,560
Yeah, they won't take our calls.

57
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:13,280
Well, I guess four of them's just going to have to be good enough.

58
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,500
Here's hoping.

59
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:22,540
No, no, no!

60
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,460
What's wrong with you?

61
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,040
What's wrong with me?

62
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,000
This is not where I should be right now.

63
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,040
That's what's wrong.

64
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:31,940
There are more important things I need to be doing.

65
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,700
Don't be ridiculous.

66
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,220
There's a Kishin out walking the Earth again.

67
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,240
What could possibly be more important than dealing with it?

68
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:42,940
You're still young. I wouldn't expect you to understand.

69
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:48,460
All I want to do is retire and find myself a good husband, but I still get all this work dumped on me.

70
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,620
Doesn't that seem unfair?

71
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,060
When there's work to be done, we don't have a choice.

72
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:57,700
I devote myself completely to every man I date, but they always end up dumping me.

73
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,860
Have you ever thought that maybe your devotion puts so much pressure on them that they feel the need to run away from you?

74
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,720
I don't understand the power of love!

75
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:14,100
Yeah, maybe you're right about that, but you don't understand the power of your punches.

76
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:15,280
Oh, sorry.

77
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:21,800
Anyway, it's old-fashioned to think that only marriage can make a woman happy.

78
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:30,600
Okay, Marie, what is it now?

79
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,460
I've decided I'm going to marry this toilet.

80
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,440
That's it. It'll be perfect.

81
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:38,740
After all, what's more accepting than a toilet?

82
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:41,900
It'll take anything and everything. It's an ideal husband.

83
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:47,000
Hold on a second. Let's just think this over.

84
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,540
Wouldn't it be annoying when the toilet seat was left up?

85
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:51,500
I can live with that. It's not a big deal.

86
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:54,220
Oh, no. I've got to stop her.

87
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:57,040
Uh, okay, but nobody's perfect.

88
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:00,300
Even the toilet might complain a bit if you put more pressure on it than it can take.

89
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:05,560
And I hate to tell you this, but he could secretly spring a leak without you knowing.

90
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,620
A leak? How indecent!

91
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,720
It's over!

92
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,760
You dirty traitor!

93
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:17,060
Okay, we can go see Lord Death now.

94
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:20,460
And Marie the Pulverizer strikes again.

95
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:23,540
She won't be retiring anytime soon.

96
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:35,860
Need something?

97
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:39,500
Yes. We need to go and check in with Lord Death.

98
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,860
Nope, I'm not going. Sorry.

99
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,120
And why's that?

100
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:45,640
Tell me this, Stein.

101
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:49,980
Why do you think Lord Death is gathering all the other death scies here at the DWMA?

102
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:55,580
Because the Kishan's revived and we need to come up with a plan quickly before it can do any more damage.

103
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:56,840
No, you're wrong.

104
00:07:57,060 --> 00:08:00,540
Lord Death's totally planning to send me away, transferred, and demoted.

105
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,080
Oh, yeah?

106
00:08:02,360 --> 00:08:03,660
I mean, think about it.

107
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:06,380
If only I'd stayed with him like I'm supposed to,

108
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,860
he would have been able to use me to defeat Asherah.

109
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:11,960
So now you're polishing sconces to earn some points with him.

110
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,420
Is that a problem?

111
00:08:13,900 --> 00:08:15,100
Wow, you are dumb.

112
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,460
Yeah, well, I'm a little desperate here, Stein.

113
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:23,500
I don't want my ex-wife to take full custody of Manka.

114
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,500
If that happens, I won't ever get to see my little girl

115
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:28,940
and then I'll hardly even feel like I'm her father anymore.

116
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,960
It already hardly seems like you are.

117
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:36,860
You're actually desperate enough to roll up your sleeves and do some hard labor.

118
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:37,580
That's right.

119
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:39,740
And I'll roll him up even more if I have to.

120
00:08:41,060 --> 00:08:41,980
Look over there.

121
00:08:42,060 --> 00:08:42,560
It's Stein.

122
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,480
Your first love.

123
00:08:43,620 --> 00:08:44,900
I don't know what you're talking about.

124
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:46,060
Hmm?

125
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:48,820
Hey, long time no see.

126
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:50,100
Hello, you two.

127
00:08:51,060 --> 00:08:51,980
It's her.

128
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:53,900
Queen of Committee Chairman.

129
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,780
You were always an annoying, bossy brat, Azusa.

130
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:02,920
Yes, I remember you complaining every time I tried to dismember a passer-by.

131
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:04,220
I'm with her on that.

132
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:10,100
Wouldn't you say the Keishan's revival was largely a result of your blundering ineptitude?

133
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:14,260
Hey, now, let's not go saying stuff like that when we're in front of Lord Death, okay?

134
00:09:14,260 --> 00:09:15,680
I don't know if that'll be possible.

135
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:18,400
I have a tendency to speak my mind at all times.

136
00:09:19,020 --> 00:09:20,380
Come to think of it, Marie,

137
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:24,420
weren't you planning to retire right after you became a Death Scythe?

138
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,200
Please don't remind me.

139
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,120
All right, there will be no more talking.

140
00:09:30,120 --> 00:09:32,260
Lord Death is waiting for us in the Death Room.

141
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,500
Everyone, line up!

142
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:34,720
Add attention!

143
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:38,700
Here we go again.

144
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:42,260
Oh, great Lord,

145
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,760
why will you not speak your magnificent words

146
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,560
that I may hear them and swiftly obey?

147
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:51,860
Oh, this is a tragedy.

148
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:54,640
I am unable to hear your voice.

149
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,140
Um, actually, you should...

150
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:58,980
Take out the earphones!

151
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,500
It's good to see you all again.

152
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:05,480
Justin, at your service as always.

153
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:11,440
Thank you for coming all this way, Death Scythes.

154
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:14,040
Now then, let's get down to business.

155
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:18,440
I assume you already know why I've called you to the DWMA on such short notice.

156
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:19,860
Please no transfer.

157
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:21,320
Please no transfer!

158
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:27,640
The Kish in Asherah, a former member of my personal guard, has revived.

159
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:30,180
Obviously, we need to discuss this.

160
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:35,020
Despite Asherah's incredible strength, he's still a big old scaredy cat.

161
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:37,480
I doubt he will make any moves this early on.

162
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:41,280
This means the most pressing task for us at the moment

163
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,920
is not determining how to counteract Asherah's actions,

164
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:47,340
but establishing a strategy for dealing with his madness wavelengths.

165
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,100
That's the real danger now.

166
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:54,000
Stein, could you answer any questions the others might have about these wavelengths?

167
00:10:54,780 --> 00:10:55,340
Yes.

168
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:57,060
What are they exactly?

169
00:10:57,500 --> 00:11:00,720
Can we consider them comparable to the sole wavelengths of the Kishin?

170
00:11:00,720 --> 00:11:04,640
Yes, but these wavelengths are on a godly level.

171
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:06,840
What makes the wavelengths so dangerous?

172
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:07,760
What can they do?

173
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:11,760
Everyone in the world possesses at least a small amount of madness.

174
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:15,200
I am no exception.

175
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:22,940
Asherah's madness wavelengths rouse the insanity that sleeps deep in people's souls, magnifying it.

176
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:26,420
The madness spreads like a disease.

177
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:30,980
I could feel the waves of it the moment Asherah was revived.

178
00:11:34,980 --> 00:11:39,620
A plague of madness.

179
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:42,700
And you're saying anybody can feel its effects?

180
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:43,960
Not quite.

181
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:48,760
It might be relatively difficult for a person like Justin to be infected by the madness.

182
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:53,700
Also, for the time being at least, I think the outbreak will be limited.

183
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:58,460
I doubt it will have much effect on ordinary people as they go about their daily business.

184
00:11:58,980 --> 00:12:01,560
Then what major problem does the madness pose initially?

185
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:03,380
It will strengthen the wicked.

186
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,560
That's correct.

187
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:09,140
For example, dismembering living things has always intrigued me.

188
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:10,900
The madness enhances that.

189
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,320
There's much more.

190
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,400
The wavelengths will awaken witches who are now dormant.

191
00:12:16,540 --> 00:12:18,340
And they will affect more than just people.

192
00:12:18,760 --> 00:12:23,440
Natural disasters, unusual weather phenomena, all sorts of horrors are possible.

193
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:27,400
Enemies who have been inactive for a long time will begin moving.

194
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:33,140
The reason we're in this situation is the blundering of these two idiots.

195
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:36,320
Lord Death, have you given any thought as to what should be done with them?

196
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,720
Why, shoot, little...

197
00:12:38,720 --> 00:12:40,580
Yes, about that.

198
00:12:42,020 --> 00:12:43,900
Anything but reassignment, please!

199
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:47,680
I'm thinking a very slight staff reassignment might be in order.

200
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:59,580
My happy life with my daughter is gone.

201
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:00,760
Gone for good.

202
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,020
What future could I ever have now?

203
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,540
How am I going to explain this to Maka?

204
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:08,860
I don't want to see that sad look on her dear little face.

205
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:10,980
No, no. Calm down, spirit.

206
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:13,200
You're still going to be my personal weapon.

207
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:16,860
Are you really going to keep me?

208
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,580
You shouldn't be so surprised.

209
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:21,740
You are the only Death Scythe who is actually a Death Scythe.

210
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,820
Have a little more confidence in yourself.

211
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:25,420
Oh, Lord.

212
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:28,040
You are a truly kind and benevolent ruler.

213
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:33,000
Recently, I've sent you off to serve as Stein's temporary weapon whenever he needed you.

214
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:34,480
That has to change.

215
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:38,620
You must avoid leaving the Academy as much as physically possible from now on.

216
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,040
Understood, sir.

217
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:41,780
One other change.

218
00:13:41,860 --> 00:13:44,680
I think we should have an additional Death Scythe stationed here

219
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:46,980
to help fortify the DWMA's defenses.

220
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:51,400
Marie, I'm assigning that duty to you.

221
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:53,960
I'd like you to be Stein's new partner.

222
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,460
Huh? Why me?

223
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,400
Oh, no!

224
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,400
Please, you can't be serious!

225
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:01,960
I've completely lost the motivation to work!

226
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,200
I even chose to be in charge of Oceania

227
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:06,360
because I knew it would be peaceful and easy!

228
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:09,000
If I'm always busy here at the Academy,

229
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:11,040
it'll take me even longer to find a husband!

230
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:12,740
It's okay.

231
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:16,240
I have a feeling your obsessive tendencies will come in handy.

232
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,380
Don't say that!

233
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:19,320
More Deaths, sir?

234
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,320
What task would you like me to take?

235
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:25,180
You'll use your wide field of vision to locate Asherah,

236
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,560
wherever he's run off to.

237
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:29,120
You'll also be in charge of Oceania

238
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:31,460
while Marie is stationed here at the school.

239
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:32,020
Right.

240
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:35,760
And as for your task, Justin...

241
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:47,160
Well, never mind Justin for now.

242
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:49,520
Obviously, life here at the DWMA

243
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,700
is going to have to change in the coming weeks.

244
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:53,600
We're entering a difficult time,

245
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:55,220
but at least it'll be exciting.

246
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,360
Okay, class dismissed.

247
00:14:58,360 --> 00:15:03,540
Oh, hang back a second, Spirit.

248
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,040
Uh...

249
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:05,760
Yes, sir.

250
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,000
There's something you and I need to discuss in private.

251
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:18,300
All right!

252
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,880
Let's play some basketball!

253
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:20,700
Yeah!

254
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,400
Hey, Maka!

255
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,820
Get over here!

256
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:26,300
Why should I?

257
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:28,980
You said you were fine with me reading a book on the sidelines.

258
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,160
That's the only reason I agreed to come.

259
00:15:31,720 --> 00:15:32,960
Well, I lied, sorry.

260
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:37,640
It's not my fault, you know.

261
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,680
Liz suddenly flaked out on us,

262
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:40,880
so now we need you to play.

263
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,500
What am I supposed to do?

264
00:15:42,620 --> 00:15:43,960
I don't know how to play this.

265
00:15:44,420 --> 00:15:44,720
Here!

266
00:15:45,020 --> 00:15:45,840
It's for your hair.

267
00:15:46,260 --> 00:15:46,900
All right.

268
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:47,660
Three on three.

269
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:48,980
These teams should work for now.

270
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:49,820
Hey, kid.

271
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:51,900
Why couldn't Liz come out and play today?

272
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:54,720
Something about nice nails that took a long time to grow.

273
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:57,340
A regular game of basketball would be boring.

274
00:15:57,740 --> 00:15:59,760
Let's say the losing captain gets a punishment.

275
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,380
That ought to make things more interesting.

276
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:03,120
Yeah, sounds good.

277
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:04,420
What are the punishments?

278
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:06,600
If we lose, we'll move the picture frames

279
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,000
and kids place two centimeters.

280
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:08,980
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

281
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:10,860
That would be interesting.

282
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:12,200
All right, and if we lose,

283
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,440
then Captain Maka here has to spend a whole day

284
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,020
hanging out with her creepy old man.

285
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:19,140
Hold on, that doesn't make any sense.

286
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,140
Don't you want to be Captain Blackstar?

287
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:22,500
You'll be the center of attention.

288
00:16:23,820 --> 00:16:24,960
It's so hard,

289
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:27,440
but I feel really bad for forcing you to play.

290
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,620
It'll be a sacrifice,

291
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:31,260
but I'll regretfully surrender my captain duties

292
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,180
to you, Maka.

293
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,020
You have to decide now not to be an attention hog?

294
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:37,200
You are wearing the captain's cap, Maka.

295
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,800
Huh? That's what you gave me.

296
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:39,820
Damn it!

297
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,480
I want to be captain!

298
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:43,260
Come with me. Let's switch.

299
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,620
Okay, here we go.

300
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:47,760
Bring it on.

301
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:47,980
Huh?

302
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:49,720
So isn't on our team.

303
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:51,480
What's he doing passing it to Blackstar?

304
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:51,920
Here.

305
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,860
Why'd Blackstar pass it back?

306
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,780
Right. Let's do it.

307
00:16:56,780 --> 00:16:58,740
Patty, Captain Maka,

308
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:00,560
Zone defense, okay?

309
00:17:00,740 --> 00:17:01,020
Okay!

310
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:01,660
Huh?

311
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:02,880
What's a zone?

312
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,660
Somebody please tell me!

313
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,260
Now we're starting?

314
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,620
Stop, you guys. Wait.

315
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:11,940
This is absolutely hopeless.

316
00:17:12,080 --> 00:17:13,220
How am I supposed to find a husband

317
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:14,520
in a place that's full of kids?

318
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:15,440
That'll be impossible.

319
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,060
Huh?

320
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:22,900
Hey, nice shooting, kid.

321
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:25,080
Are they students from the DWMA?

322
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,120
Yes.

323
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,440
And they're your students starting tomorrow.

324
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,220
That was a foul, Maka.

325
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,600
You can't double dribble the ball.

326
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:33,400
Come on.

327
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:34,200
You're the captain.

328
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,260
Shouldn't you know better?

329
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,020
Huh?

330
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:36,900
I don't get it.

331
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:37,940
What's a double dribble?

332
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,580
I mean, it sounds kind of cool.

333
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:43,680
Okay.

334
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,380
I don't have a boyfriend right now anyway.

335
00:17:46,540 --> 00:17:48,100
I guess I might as well do some work.

336
00:17:48,780 --> 00:17:49,500
Oh, yeah.

337
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,000
I forgot.

338
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:51,980
Everything's happened so quickly.

339
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:53,360
I'll need to stay at your place

340
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:55,140
until I can find an apartment in town.

341
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:56,380
That's fine.

342
00:17:56,460 --> 00:17:58,380
But don't blame me if you wind up dismembered.

343
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,260
I have complete faith in you.

344
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,240
What is it, sir?

345
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:07,100
Actually, I need to talk to you about Stine.

346
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,600
I'm pretty sure he's realized it himself.

347
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,760
But his old madness is beginning to take hold of him again.

348
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:17,820
So you put him with Marie?

349
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,660
I think she's the best partner for him right now.

350
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,180
Her soul wavelength should have a positive effect

351
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,760
on the madness inside him.

352
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:28,860
So, Spirit, you're Stine's former partner.

353
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:32,700
Can I ask you to keep an eye on his situation for me as well?

354
00:18:33,100 --> 00:18:33,420
Yes.

355
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:37,780
Jeez.

356
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:41,200
Is he always going to be this much of a headache?

357
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,480
Stay close to me, Patty.

358
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:43,640
Huh?

359
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:44,840
Hey.

360
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:47,020
Oh, I didn't see you there, Spirit.

361
00:18:47,020 --> 00:18:50,200
What are they doing here?

362
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:53,080
Didn't we tell them to stay at home so they can heal?

363
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,820
I'm always amazed by how carefree kids can be.

364
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,320
You guys are about to see something special.

365
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:02,020
I wouldn't call it carefree.

366
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:05,320
They just had the biggest battle of their lives.

367
00:19:05,900 --> 00:19:08,680
They're trying to regain some normalcy in their own way.

368
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:11,200
Game over.

369
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:13,080
Final score, 20 to 4.

370
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:14,280
Maka's team loses.

371
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,020
We never even figured out how to play the game.

372
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:18,220
Punishment!

373
00:19:19,300 --> 00:19:19,820
Punishment!

374
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:21,380
Punishment!

375
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:22,720
Glad it's not me.

376
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:25,100
Maybe we should let her off the hook.

377
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,260
I'm not so sure about that.

378
00:19:27,980 --> 00:19:30,500
This doesn't seem much more normal than that fight underground.

379
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:33,560
It's still two sides fighting for different goals.

380
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:34,780
Jeez, Stine.

381
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:38,580
A simple game like basketball, and you still just can't quite get it, can you?

382
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:43,440
Oh.

383
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:45,360
Hey, what's going on, Maka?

384
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:50,920
Um, you see, Papa, do you want to hang out?

385
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:52,500
Like, Saturday?

386
00:19:52,500 --> 00:20:04,920
I never thought this day would come, to think I almost got sent away today!

387
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:08,200
Hey, Papa, which do you want, strawberry or banana?

388
00:20:09,160 --> 00:20:11,500
Which shirt do you think will look better on me?

389
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:13,180
It's cold out.

390
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,140
Thanks, Papa.

391
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:15,800
It's so nice and warm.

392
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:19,500
I thought Maka was looking for normalcy!

393
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,500
Papa?

394
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,580
What's wrong, Papa?

395
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:28,460
Are you okay?

396
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:31,660
Sorry.

397
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:33,960
It's just that I'm so happy.

398
00:20:34,820 --> 00:20:35,560
Hang on.

399
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:37,200
I'll get some medicine for you.

400
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,260
No, it's really, I'm okay.

401
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,080
Shoot me now.

402
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:43,980
Happy puking.

403
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:47,820
I guess that's one more thing I don't understand.

404
00:20:47,820 --> 00:20:51,640
Or death.

405
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,680
You put it off before,

406
00:20:54,820 --> 00:20:57,520
but I think we need to decide what to do with the demon sword.

407
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,100
All right, then.

408
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,660
I've made up my mind.

409
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:02,720
We'll enroll him in the academy.

410
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:04,000
Seriously?

411
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:06,320
Yes, of course, seriously.

412
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:08,580
Really, not joking.

413
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:09,580
That's my decision.

414
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:13,940
The kid has some major issues we'll have to deal with, I know.

415
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:16,060
But if we guide him carefully enough,

416
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:18,800
he'll become an excellent ally for the DWMA.

417
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:22,380
We could really use someone like him on our side right now.

418
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:23,540
I understand.

419
00:21:24,100 --> 00:21:26,640
But he's still in no condition to enroll in classes.

420
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,080
I agree with you.

421
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:31,500
That's why we'll move slowly.

422
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:35,360
His trial enrollment in the academy begins tomorrow.

423
00:21:35,360 --> 00:22:05,340
We'll be right back.

424
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:35,340
We'll be right back.

425
00:22:35,360 --> 00:23:05,340
We'll be right back.

426
00:23:05,360 --> 00:23:07,360
We'll be right back.

427
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:07,860
Yes.

428
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:11,360
Finally, all the seemingly unrelated incidents are connected.

429
00:23:11,420 --> 00:23:12,280
No, not that.

430
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:14,360
Do you mean the link between global warming and human overuse?

431
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,440
No, no, no.

432
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,600
Okay, what then?

433
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:18,160
Are you doing a connect the dots puzzle?

434
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,380
Please, come on.

435
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,020
Then maybe...

436
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:22,080
If you'll shut up for a second, I'll say it.

437
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,440
The hip bone's connected to the leg bone.

438
00:23:24,980 --> 00:23:25,800
Um, Asuza?

439
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:27,900
On the next episode of Soul Eater,

440
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:30,420
the exciting and embarrassing trial enrollment,

441
00:23:30,880 --> 00:23:33,500
the DWMA new lifestyle support fair is open?

442
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:35,120
Totally stole my thunder.

